---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { calculators, categoryOrder, categoryLabels } from '../../data/calculators';

const categoryCounts = categoryOrder.map((category) => ({
  label: categoryLabels[category].en,
  count: calculators.filter((c) => c.category === category).length,
}));
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why Comzip Calculators exists and how it's run."
  path="/about"
  lang="en"
>
  <h1>About Comzip Calculators</h1>

  <p>
    Comzip Calculators is a free site that brings together the calculators
    you end up needing at some point in everyday life — Korean age, salary,
    taxes, real estate, and more. Instead of searching around for a
    calculator with the right assumptions every time, you can run the
    calculation here and see exactly how the result was derived.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Every time I needed to calculate take-home pay, acquisition tax, or my
    Korean age, I kept running into sites cluttered with ads, calculators
    with unclear methodology, or pages that were awkward to use on mobile —
    so I started building my own. This is an independently run side project,
    and the number of calculators keeps growing.
  </p>

  <h2>How it's run</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No sign-up — everything runs in your browser.</strong> Values
      you enter are never sent to or stored on a server; they're processed
      entirely on your device. See the
      <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Calculations cite their basis.</strong> Tax and legal
      calculators list the specific statute and the date it was last checked
      at the bottom of the page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Korean and English are both supported.</strong> New calculators
      are built with both language versions from the start.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What's covered right now</h2>
  <p>
    {calculators.length} calculators across {categoryOrder.length} categories:{' '}
    {categoryCounts.map(({ label, count }) => `${label} (${count})`).join(', ')}.
    Browse the full list by category or search on the <a href="/en/">homepage</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If a result looks off, a law has changed, or you'd like to see a new
    calculator added, let me know.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email: <a href="mailto:comzip@gmail.com">comzip@gmail.com</a></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    All results are for reference only and carry no legal effect. Before
    filing, paying, or processing payroll, always confirm with the relevant
    authority (National Tax Service, Hometax, Ministry of Employment and
    Labor, etc.).
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
